The 175-row algebraic witness passes exactly those 175 equations, but the floor gate catches a second semantic omission: 94 older selected coefficients (bands ≤24) become nonzero. The newly free variables include D23/D25 coordinates that the parked presentation had eliminated and should have been reconstructed, not reintroduced as independent D43 coordinates. So the explicit 34+52+89 union is NONEMPTY, but it is still an overapproximation and cannot honestly receive a floor. I’m now following the existing symbolic reconstruction DAG to test the genuinely lifted A¹⁴ family; this is the same fail-closed issue the floor requirement is designed to expose.
